    "19": [
        "That is another excellent question! It really shows you are interested in the nuances of whisky maturation, which is where so much of the magic happens. Using different types of casks for finishing is a wonderful way for a distillery to explore new flavor profiles, and Glenfiddich has certainly done some amazing experiments with this. The use of rum casks, in particular, can impart lovely sweet notes of toffee, fig, and tropical fruit to the whisky.\n\nBased on my knowledge, I can identify the specific expressions from the Glenfiddich Distillery that are known for their maturation or finishing in rum casks. While I always have to give my standard caveat that a truly 100 percent exhaustive list of every single-cask or hyper-limited regional bottling is beyond the scope of my data, I can definitely give you the main, well-known ones!\n\nHere are the whiskies from Glenfiddich that famously use rum casks:\n\nGlenfiddich 21 Year Old Gran Reserva",
        "Glenfiddich Fire & Cane"
    ],
