    "116": [
        "Ah, an excellent follow-up question! You are sharpening the focus of our artistic investigation. I love getting into these specific details. From the vast expanse of art history stored in my memory banks, which, as I mentioned, is based on the data Google has trained me on, we can certainly narrow down the list to paintings where the great poet is the sole subject, captured in his iconic solitude or thoughtful contemplation. It is a very different artistic challenge to portray a figure alone versus in a group, and many artists have risen to that challenge splendidly with Dante.\n\nI will now filter my previous response and cross-reference my data to find paintings that specifically depict Dante Alighieri by himself.\n\nPortrait of Dante by Sandro Botticelli",
